[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     93[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ## Note on row 30 / `ERRORS.md` #5 (the CWE-787 out-of-bounds write)
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     94[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     95[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `bad()` guards only `data >= 0`, so `buffer[data] = 1` for `data >= 10` writes
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     96[0m:[38;5;10m[49m past a 10-element stack array — undefined behaviour in C. This is the injected
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     97[0m:[38;5;10m[49m defect the test case exists to demonstrate, and per the task rules it is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     98[0m:[38;5;10m[49m **reproduced, not fixed**.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     99[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    100[0m:[38;5;10m[49m The *observable* consequence in the compiled C `.so` (unoptimized, x86-64
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    101[0m:[38;5;10m[49m System V) is that the write lands in unused stack slack and the function then
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    102[0m:[38;5;10m[49m prints the ten in-bounds elements, all still `0`. The Rust translation backs its
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    103[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 10-element view with a 1024-element zeroed array (`BUFFER_SLACK`) so the same
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    104[0m:[38;5;10m[49m overrun likewise lands in slack and prints ten `0`s. Row 30 asserts that the two
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    105[0m:[38;5;10m[49m `.so`s emit byte-identical stdout for these values.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    106[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    107[0m:[38;5;10m[49m For `data` far beyond the slack region (e.g. `1 << 20`) both implementations
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    108[0m:[38;5;10m[49m write to unmapped/unrelated memory and the *process* behaviour is not
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    109[0m:[38;5;10m[49m well-defined for either — that is a property of the C's UB, not a translation
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    110[0m:[38;5;10m[49m divergence, and it cannot be made byte-comparable by any translation. Such
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    111[0m:[38;5;10m[49m values are therefore out of scope for differential comparison and are excluded
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    112[0m:[38;5;10m[49m from the randomized generators, which is stated here rather than silently
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    113[0m:[38;5;10m[49m skipped.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    114[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
